      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CLANG AND BANG (8) was quickly into stride on debut to score by 3 lengths (17.07) at this track over 300m. Boxed wide but has the pace to be prominent. Looks the one to beat. COOL MIST (7) has a solid record despite not breaking through for a win in 43 starts. Was below best last time when missed the frame finishing second (17.28) at this track. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings six times from eight starts. Winning chance. MARLENE JENICE (6) showed little early speed at her last couple, the latest finishing fifth (20.27) in a Grade 5 at Grafton. Speedy beginner who can find the front despite the tricky draw. Better than the latest run and deserves another chance. HOT BETTY (2) is a Shane Staples-trained newcomer by Aston Rupee out of Miss Integrity. Gets every chance from the inside draw. Can sneak into the frame at her first appearance.",
